From 41ca81cd93cc6954b0d752bb2718ccac898a52d0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 02:38:45 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(kanban): keep scratch files named in handoff metadata
 past workspace cleanup [daveey]

Workers cite workspace files in kanban_complete / request_review metadata
(replay_report=<ws>/REPORT.md, plan=<ws>/PLAN.md). Completion reaps the
managed scratch workspace right after, and only metadata["artifacts"] was
copied out, so reviewers found those citations dangling (t_01a19d7fc2cfe36a,
t_01a19d0bcab45558 on 2026-11-02).

_stage_completion_artifacts now also runs kanban_metadata_files.preserve_metadata_files:
every regular file under the managed scratch workspace that a metadata string
names is copied into attachments/<task> (20 MiB total), recorded as an
attachment row, the string rewritten to the copy, and attached_from_workspace
maps original -> copy. A file that can't be kept (over the cap, missing, a
dir, copy error) is skipped with a logged warning and recorded under
attached_from_workspace_skipped; it never fails the transition. Paths outside
the workspace are untouched; a file both declared and named is copied once.
